        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5df4ad71-08b9-5b96-ae47-81a2e9ef7a53",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Wagner, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Set Svanholm, Lorenzo Quaglio\n- Works: Siegfried, Der Ring des Nibelungen, Idomeneo\n- Places: Mannheim, Munich\n- Roles: operatic tenor\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Wagner composed Siegfried, WWV 86C, as the third of the four music dramas in Der Ring des Nibelungen.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart composed Idomeneo, K. 366, as an Italian-language opera seria.\n- Lorenzo Quaglio worked mainly in Mannheim and Munich, and he designed the first production of Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart's opera Idomeneo in Munich.\n- Set Svanholm was a Swedish operatic tenor who was considered the leading Tristan and Siegfried of the first decade after World War II.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f9f859e7-036a-51af-9ffd-8a05513fa9b7",
        "text": "Page: Siegfried (opera). Sentence: Siegfried, WWV 86C, is the third of the four music dramas that constitute \"Der Ring des Nibelungen\" (\"The Ring of the Nibelung\"), by Richard Wagner.\nPage: Idomeneo. Sentence: Idomeneo, re di Creta ossia Ilia e Idamante (Italian for \"Idomeneus, King of Crete, or, Ilia and Idamante\"; usually referred to simply as Idomeneo, K. 366) is an Italian language opera seria by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart.\nPage: Set Svanholm. Sentence: Set Svanholm (2 September 19044 October 1964) was a Swedish operatic tenor, considered the leading Tristan and Siegfried of the first decade following World War II.\nPage: Lorenzo Quaglio. Sentence: He worked mainly in Mannheim and in Munich, where he designed the first production of Mozart's opera \"Idomeneo\".",
